\section{Clock-Certificate Statistics}
\label{sec:cert_supp}

Over the $4\,320$ operating-region trials of the internal SNR suite, all
$35\,696$ conditional clock profiles satisfy the prescribed tolerance; the
largest $g_{\rm cert}/\epsilon_{\rm clk}$ over all visited positions is
$0.999957$.

The median outer evaluation count is $8$, no Powell safeguard is selected,
and panel pairing is correct on all operating-region trials. Two trials
are catastrophic. A valid conditional certificate bounds clock
optimization error at the tested position; it does not bound statistical
estimation error or certify the outer position search.

\section{Resource Scaling}
\label{sec:scaling_supp}

Resource sweeps vary $N,T,M_A,M_R,K$ individually. Proposed conditional
RMSE decreases from $2.02$ to $0.426$~mm as $M_R$ grows from $16^2$ to
$64^2$, from $0.884$ to $0.360$~mm as $M_A$ grows from $4$ to $24$, and
from $1.25$ to $0.426$~mm as $T$ grows from $32$ to $256$.
Across the $19$ settings its catastrophic rate lies in $[0,2.71]\%$ and
is no larger than the control's. At $K=4$ the rates are $2.71\%$ and
$12.29\%$. These sweeps use one infrastructure layout.

The serialized benchmark mean is $3.18$~s with peak RSS $2.52$~GB
(Table~\ref{tab:s_cost}). A separate $30$-trial decomposition
gives a sum of component medians of $3.16$~s: $0.229$~s for projection,
$0.845$~s for common geometry, $0.086$~s for anchor refresh, $0.339$~s for
Phase~II and $1.666$~s for the remaining Phase-I blocks, the last value
aggregating several operations. That decomposition run peaks at $3.25$~GB,
above the $2.52$~GB of the serialized measurement reported in
Table~\ref{tab:s_cost}.

